#
# Declarative example-conformance fixtures for the learning slice — the test-DSL
# twin of the SHACL pytest in tests/test_learning.py ("this Teaching must
# validate, that counter-example must be rejected"). The harness
# (crates/slicetest run_conformance_cell) validates learning/module.ttl + the one
# bound gmeow:exampleFile against learning/shapes.ttl (gmeow:TeachingShape) and
# compares finding codes.
#
# MESSAGE→CODE shift: the original pytest asserted a specific sh:message substring;
# these cells pin the constraint-component CODE (shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>).
# This is the lossy shift the concepts/epistemics exemplars accepted: the code form
# COLLAPSES distinct sh:message strings that share a constraint component. Because
# each counter-example is a SEPARATE fixture isolating ONE violation, the
# (fixture, code) pair still pins the specific constraint faithfully.
#
# CODE VERIFICATION (two-way, 2026-06-23): every expectedViolationCode below was
# confirmed by running the native validator (via `make slicetest`) on
# module + fixture + shapes and reading the FULL emitted code-set — each violator
# emits EXACTLY its one expected code and NO other finding (the harness's
# gmeow:violates check is a CONTAINS, so the singleton was confirmed by a
# sentinel-flip to guard against a stray second violation masking a malformed
# fixture). The teacher==learner case fires only the sh:sparql rule (all
# min/maxCount + sh:class constraints are satisfied); the non-agent-learner case
# fires only the learner sh:class rule (learner minCount 1 is satisfied by ex:tool).
#
# The conforming fixture lives under tests/conformance-fixtures/ (NOT examples/)
# and the counter-examples under tests/counter-examples/, so the global
# `make validate` gate never loads them as data; they are validated SLICE-SCOPED
# only (module + slice shapes), intentional and mirroring the concepts precedent.
#
# See dsl/tests/MIGRATION-LEDGER.md for the per-test pytest→DSL mapping.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/learning/tests/> .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed Teaching -------------------------------------
ex:ecTeachingConforms a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/teaching-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture supplies exactly one gmeow:teacher (a gmeow:Agent), one distinct gmeow:learner (a gmeow:Agent), and a gmeow:subjectTaught, so it satisfies gmeow:TeachingShape and validates with no findings. Mirrors test_wellformed_teaching_conforms." .

# --- Violating: teacher equals learner (an agent cannot teach itself) --------
ex:ecTeachingSelf a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/teaching-self.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSoleFinding true ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's gmeow:teacher and gmeow:learner are the same agent (ex:alice). gmeow:TeachingShape's sh:sparql constraint forbids teacher = learner, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. Mirrors test_teacher_equals_learner_is_flagged." .

# --- Violating: learner is not a gmeow:Agent --------------------------------
ex:ecTeachingNonAgentLearner a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/teaching-non-agent-learner.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.ClassConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSoleFinding true ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's gmeow:learner (ex:tool) is a gmeow:Artifact, not a gmeow:Agent. The learner property shape carries sh:class gmeow:Agent, so validation MUST emit shacl.ClassConstraintComponent and NO other finding. Mirrors test_non_agent_learner_is_flagged." .
